unt‑1, so a sub‑schema is finally created and returned.'}]}, {'group': 'Sub‑schema found – id is null but segment is the last one', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'fragment', 'value': 'JsonNodePath representing /singleLevel'}], 'expected': 'Returns a JsonSchema instance for the node at "/singleLevel" even though the resolved id is null, because the segment is the last one.', 'description': 'When the fragment consists of a single segment, the loop runs once (x == 0 == nameCount‑1). The condition `((id != null) || (x == nameCount‑1))` evaluates to true, forcing creation of the sub‑schema despite a null id.'}]}, {'group': 'Fragment not found – fetchSubSchemaNode returns null (exception path)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'fragment', 'value': 'JsonNodePath representing /nonexistent'}], 'expected': 'InvalidSchemaRefException is thrown with a ValidationMessage of type REF and code internal.unresolvedRef.', 'description': 'The fragment cannot be resolved in the current document. `subSchemaNode` is null, `document.findSchemaResourceRoot().fetchSubSchemaNode` returns null, so the method throws an InvalidSchemaRefException.'}]}, {'group': 'Fragment not found – fetchSubSchemaNode returns a schema that can resolve the fragment', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'fragment', 'value': 'JsonNodePath representing /externalRef'}], 'expected': 'Returns the JsonSchema obtained from the recursive call `found.getSubSchema(fragment)`.', 'description': 'When the fragment is not present in the current document, the method delegates to the root schema resource (`document.findSchemaResourceRoot().fetchSubSchemaNode`). That call returns a non‑null JsonSchema (`found`), which then successfully resolves the fragment via its own `getSubSchema` call, and the resulting sub‑schema is returned.'}]}, {'group': 'Intermediate sub‑schema created because $id is present', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'fragment', 'value': 'JsonNodePath representing /components/schemas/User/properties/id'}